{"id":237670312432526,"type":"artist","name":"Guru Guru","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":16,"info":{"img":"https://cdn-images.dzcdn.net/images/artist/0d597dec074dbbd616fca0f897d81e04/1000x1000-000000-80-0-0.jpg","bio":"En 1966 Mani Neumeier (batería y voz) se encontraba tocando junto a Uli Trepte (bajo y voz) en una banda de free jazz el Irene Swch Trío, entusiasmados con sus influencias musicales, clásicas, contemporáneas, Hendrix, Pink Floyd y la música de India deciden formar una banda que contemplara mejor estas inquietudes. En 1968 forman Guru Guru Groove con la firme convicción de hacer “free rock”, luego de varios cambios de integrantes incorporan a Ax Genrich en guitarra y voz y en 1970 ya como Guru Guru","tags":["krautrock","Progressive rock","Psychedelic Rock","psychedelic","experimental"]},"works":[{"id":211108739647360,"type":"song","name":"Der LSD Marsch","artist":"Guru Guru","year":1970,"weight":6,"yt":"FOy1647ptng","src":"books","from":{"books":[{"name":"Scaruffi","title":"A History of Rock Music 1951-2000 (Piero Scaruffi)"}],"podcasts":[],"lists":[],"n_lists":0}},{"id":123220535107452,"type":"album","name":"UFO","artist":"Guru Guru","year":1970,"weight":3,"yt":"r1RaaFOb66M","src":"musthear","from":{"books":[],"podcasts":[],"lists":[{"id":23428794615065,"name":"RYM Top — Rock — Krautrock","rank":141,"scaruffi":null}],"n_lists":1}},{"id":234051057502797,"type":"album","name":"Hinten","artist":"Guru Guru","year":1971,"weight":7,"yt":"DrpWBvIpvmM","src":"musthear","from":{"books":[],"podcasts":[],"lists":[{"id":23428794615065,"name":"RYM Top — Rock — Krautrock","rank":68,"scaruffi":null},{"id":28712889142764,"name":"RYM Top — Rock — Jam Band","rank":46,"scaruffi":null},{"id":40863274011446,"name":"RYM Top — Rock — Acid Rock","rank":31,"scaruffi":null}],"n_lists":3}},{"id":173999311452121,"type":"album","name":"Känguru","artist":"Guru Guru","year":1972,"weight":5,"yt":"F0zO5ujSjx0","src":"musthear","from":{"books":[],"podcasts":[],"lists":[{"id":234287